    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0641" n="549" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg549"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Food Administrator’s File</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador on Special Mission</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Reading</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Food
                        Administrator</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hoover</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 16, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hoover</hi>: I have to-day received a reply
                    to the telegram which was despatched to London after the discussion on Thursday
                    last of your proposals about wheat. I am glad to be able to tell you that the
                    Wheat Executive agree to the supply of 2,000,000 bushels of Canadian wheat for
                    the Buffalo mills in May, as a final allocation of Canadian wheat for this
                    cereal year. They say that they are naturally reluctant that the supply of bulk
                    wheat should be reduced, but they warmly appreciate the efforts you are making
                    to increase the supply available for export in the coming months, and are
                    therefore most anxious to assist as far as practicable in the solution of your
                    distribution problem.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reading</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
